<title>NEW ZEALAND: CRICKET-NORTHERN DISTRICTS 126 RUNS BEHIND ENGLAND.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-NORTHERN DISTRICTS 126 RUNS BEHIND ENGLAND.</headline>
<dateline>HAMILTON, New Zealand 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern  Districts trailed England by 126 runs with nine second innings wickets standing at stumps on the second day of their four-day cricket match on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scores:</p>
<p>Northern Districts 69 and 99-1 (B. Pocock 60 not out).</p>
<p>England 294 (G. Thorpe 71, J. Crawley 65).</p>
